---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = "Miami Investor Loan Review | DSCR, Rental & LLC Mortgage Planning";
const description = "Request a Miami investor loan review for DSCR loans, rental property loans, Airbnb scenarios, LLC vesting, and investment property financing.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
<main id="main"><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Investor review funnel</p><h1>Miami Investor Loan Review</h1><p>Compare investor loan options based on rental income, property type, occupancy, entity structure, down payment, reserves, and exit strategy.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Scenario Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Calculate Payment</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami-Dade focused</span></div></div><form class="lead-form"><h2>Miami Investor Loan Review Form</h2><p>Share the basics so the right mortgage path can be reviewed.</p><label>Mortgage goal<select><option>Select one</option><option>Purchase</option><option>Refinance</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Condo review</option><option>Investor / DSCR</option><option>Self-employed borrower</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Property city<input placeholder="Miami, Brickell, Doral..."></label><label>Property type<select><option>Select one</option><option>Single-family</option><option>Condo</option><option>Townhome</option><option>Multi-unit</option><option>Investment property</option></select></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Price or value<input placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input placeholder="10%, 20%, $100k..."></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit range<select><option>Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720-759</option><option>680-719</option><option>640-679</option><option>600-639</option></select></label><label>Income type<select><option>Select type</option><option>W-2</option><option>Self-employed</option><option>1099</option><option>Investor / rental</option><option>Foreign national</option></select></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input></label><label>Phone<input></label></div><label>Email<input type="email"></label><label>Notes<textarea rows="4" placeholder="Condo building, deadline, loan questions..."></textarea></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="button">Send Scenario</button></form></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>Miami Investor Loan Review is designed for Miami-Dade borrowers who want a cleaner answer before they apply, submit an offer, lock a rate, or compare lenders. The goal is to turn a vague mortgage question into a structured scenario with property type, price, down payment, credit range, income documentation, city, and timeline.</p><p>Investor loans in Miami can involve DSCR, conventional investment property financing, portfolio options, foreign national investor loans, short-term rental restrictions, condo rules, and entity/title planning.</p><p>The goal is to give you enough detail to trust the process, then point you to a quote, preapproval, the calculator, or the right guide for your situation.</p><h2>Who should use this mortgage review path</h2><p>Use this page when the borrower has a specific mortgage question but is not ready for a full application. It is especially useful for borrowers comparing programs, buying a condo, changing down payment assumptions, or trying to understand how payment and cash to close will look in Miami-Dade.</p><p>For investor loan, a short form is not enough unless the right questions are asked. The page should collect the property city, property type, loan purpose, estimated price or value, down payment or equity, credit range, income type, occupancy, and timing.</p><p>The review should not promise approval or a rate. It should identify which loan programs are worth comparing and what documents or property details are needed before a reliable quote can be issued.</p><h2>What should be reviewed before quoting</h2><p>An investor loan review should focus on rental income support, property type, occupancy/rental plan, down payment, reserves, insurance, HOA rules, DSCR calculation, and whether the loan will close in an LLC.</p><p>For Miami condos, the review should include HOA dues, master insurance, project status, reserves, litigation, special assessments, rental restrictions, and whether the loan program fits the building. For jumbo or self-employed files, reserves and documentation can be just as important as the rate.</p><p>The best lead experience is a guided scenario review: borrowers answer only the questions needed for their situation, then receive a next-step recommendation instead of a generic sales pitch.</p><h2>Documents and details that improve accuracy</h2><p>Prepare address if available, estimated rent or lease, purchase price, down payment, entity documents if using an LLC, HOA/rental rules, insurance assumptions, and whether the property is short-term or long-term rental.</p><p>A buyer does not need to upload everything just to start, but the more accurate the scenario, the more useful the response. Estimated taxes, HOA dues, insurance assumptions, credit score range, and target closing date are especially important in Miami-Dade.</p><p>If the borrower is already under contract, the property address, contract price, association dues, deadline dates, and building information should be collected immediately.</p></article><aside><div class="content-card"><h2>Useful related paths</h2><ul><li><a href="dscr-loans-miami.html">DSCR Loans Miami</a></li><li><a href="rental-property-loans-miami.html">Rental Property Loans Miami</a></li><li><a href="llc-mortgage-loans-miami.html">LLC Mortgage Loans Miami</a></li><li><a href="start.html">Request a Mortgage Quote</a></li><li><a href="get-preapproved-miami.html">Get Preapproved in Miami</a></li><li><a href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Florida Mortgage Calculator</a></li><li><a href="miami-mortgage-guides.html">Miami Mortgage Guides</a></li><li><a href="mortgage-broker-miami.html">Mortgage Broker Miami</a></li></ul></div></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Send the scenario before you make the mortgage decision.</h2><p>Use the quote or preapproval path to compare payment, cash to close, property review, and documentation needs.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Miami Investor Loan Review FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is miami investor loan review the same as a loan application?</summary><p>No. A scenario review or checklist is an early planning step. A full application, documentation, credit review, underwriting, appraisal, title, insurance, and property review may still be required.</p></details><details><summary>Can this page guarantee approval or a specific interest rate?</summary><p>No. Loan approval, rate, terms, closing costs, and program availability depend on lender guidelines, documentation, underwriting, property review, market conditions, and timing.</p></details><details><summary>Should I use the calculator before requesting a quote?</summary><p>Yes. A calculator can help estimate payment, but a quote should also review taxes, homeowners insurance, flood or wind coverage, HOA dues, mortgage insurance, closing costs, and cash to close.</p></details><details><summary>What is the fastest next step?</summary><p>Submit a mortgage scenario with property city, purpose, price or value, down payment or equity, credit range, income type, and timeline. If you are shopping soon, request preapproval before making an offer.</p></details></div></div></section></main>
</BaseLayout>
